Passing Class to functions:-
    1. We have to declare the function outside main.
    2.Classes are passed by reference.

Classes in different file:-
    Class can be created in different file but have to be in the same package.

    Class can be created in different package but has to be imported by using the statement "import packageName.className;"

Access Modifiers:-
    1. Public:- all packages
    2. Private:- same class
    3. Default:- same package

Getter:-
    These are used to get the value of an element with private scope to return their value. We create a function in the same class that returns
    the value of private element.

Setter:-
    These are used to set the value of an element with private scope to change their value. We create a function that that takes a parameter,
    in the same class and change that elements value.

final Keyword:-
    Used to assign a value to any element which cannot be changed.

static functions:-
    Used if we want to access a function in the class through just className.functionName